            <ArticleTitle>Iridium-Catalyzed Enantioselective Synthesis of Dihydroimidazoquinazolinones by Elaborate Tuning of Chiral Cyclic Ligands.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6376-6379</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03230</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A highly efficient, enantioselective intramolecular allylation of (E)-4-(alkyl(4-oxo-3,4-dihydroquinazolin-2-yl)amino)but-2-en-1-yl methyl carbonates was developed, and the corresponding dihydroimidazoquinazolinones were prepared in high yields and enantiomeric excess. The allylation was performed under catalysis of iridium-chiral cyclic phosphoramidite complexes, in which the reactivity and enantioselectivity of the substrates were elaborately tuned by our developed chiral cyclic phosphoramidite ligands with adjustable sizes of rings.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
